  englishPhrases:
  - "The models use different image domains. Tea operates natively at 28\xD728 with
    training pixels in 0..1. Legacy maps MNIST to \u22121..1 and pads it to 32\xD732
    with \u22121. A 32, 64, or 128 pixel display only enlarges the native output;
    it cannot add model detail. Players share the model version, digit, seed, step
    count, and progress, while each GPU recomputes its own image and activation textures.
    Floating-point differences can cause small pixel variations. Legacy clips x_0
    to \u22121..1 and recomputes epsilon before updating; Tea does not clip."
  - "Tea's U-Net processes feature maps at 28\xD728, 14\xD714, and 7\xD77, compresses
    them to a 1\xD71 summary, then upsamples toward 28\xD728. At 14\xD714 and 28\xD728,
    the decoder concatenates matching encoder features through skip connections,
    preserving spatial cues. Each operator writes its actual result into single-precision
    RFloat textures; channels are laid out side by side. Highlight the running operator,
    its skip edge, and one activation channel to follow the computation."
  - "The forward process defines a noisy state: x_t = \u221A\u03B1\u0304_t x_0 +
    \u221A(1\u2212\u03B1\u0304_t)\u03B5, with \u03B5 sampled from a standard normal
    distribution. During training, the model sees x_t, time t, and a digit label,
    then learns to predict \u03B5. Generation starts from Gaussian noise instead
    of a known image and repeatedly uses the predicted noise to estimate a clean
    image and the next state. The changing pictures and values come from this model's
    live GPU textures."
  - "The conditional branch predicts \u03B5_c for the chosen digit; the null branch
    predicts \u03B5_null with the class masked. This build combines them as \u03B5_guided
    = \u03B5_null + 3(\u03B5_c \u2212 \u03B5_null), equivalent to the paper's (1+w)\u03B5_c
    \u2212 w\u03B5_null with w=2. Then x_0 = (x_t \u2212 \u221A(1\u2212\u03B1\u0304_t)\u03B5_guided)/\u221A\u03B1\u0304_t,
    and \u03B7=0 gives x_next = \u221A\u03B1\u0304_next x_0 + \u221A(1\u2212\u03B1\u0304_next)\u03B5_guided,
    without fresh noise. Tea uses 64 evenly spaced steps from t=400 to 1; the last
    update returns x_0."
  - "LIVE OPERATOR GRAPH \xB7 cyan: active \xB7 gold: skip \xB7 signed range \xB13"
  - "CLASS-CONDITIONAL U-NET \xB7 DDIM \xB7 FRAGMENT SHADER INFERENCE"
  - "PIXEL PROBE \xB7 completes with a denoise step"
  - Catching up to shared state; please wait
  - Shared settings / local GPU inference
  - Control requested; waiting for grant
  - Incompatible model/protocol version
  - floating-point results may differ
